Assembler Version 00b
=====================
Assembled by: Version 00

Features Supported by This Assembler
-------------------------------------
A stage between 00 and 01: DATA directives with labels and strings, in the
same syntax as version 01, so its input is also valid input for 01 and 02.
Labels are single characters, which needs no token buffer, no compare and
no search: a label's character, doubled, indexes a table of addresses.

- DATA directive, on a line that starts with a space:
    DATA $XX ...        - emit hex bytes (two upper-case hex digits)
    DATA "string"       - emit ASCII characters (no escape sequences)
    DATA name           - emit a label's 16-bit address (little-endian)
    Mixed: DATA $20 name "text" $00 on the same line
- Labels:
  - Defined by a name at column 0, bound to the program counter. The rest
    of the line is ignored.
  - Only the first character of a name counts, both where it is defined and
    where it is used, so names must differ in their first character. A
    name in DATA ends at a space or the end of the line, as in 01.
  - The table is at $3000, two bytes per character at offset 2 * character.
    A high byte of zero means undefined (labels are always at $2000 or
    above).
  - Forward references are NOT supported (single-pass)
- Semicolon comments (to end of line). Whitespace is spaces only, as in 01.
- Output starts at $2000 (hardcoded). The source's last two bytes are the
  reset vector.

Error handling (BRK with an exit code and message, as in version 01):
  - Error 01: Duplicate label (including two names with the same first
    character)
  - Error 02: Opcode not found (an indented line that does not start with D)
  - Error 03: Label not found

New in this version (relative to version 00):
- Program counter tracking
- Single-character labels, defined at column 0 and used in DATA
- String arguments in DATA
- Error reporting via BRK with inline messages

